        timingType: "Chain (Located at the REAR of the engine block. The S68 engine utilizes a completely redesigned, highly robust timing chain system located at the rear of the block, fundamentally shifting the architecture from previous M V8s. A major innovation is the use of Electronic VANOS (eVANOS), which replaces oil-pressure-driven actuators with electric motors, vastly reducing the timing system's sensitivity to oil pressure fluctuations and ensuring incredibly precise camshaft phasing.)", injectionType: "Dual Injection (A revolutionary and massively welcomed update. The S68 utilizes both High-Pressure Direct Injection (350 bar) directly into the cylinders AND Low-Pressure Port Injection into the intake manifold. This brilliant dual-system design permanently eliminates the notorious intake valve carbon buildup that plagued the previous N63/S63 engines, as the port injectors continuously wash the intake valves with fresh fuel.)", engineLifespan: "250,000+ km (The S68B44T0 is an absolute engineering marvel. The closed-deck aluminum block is virtually indestructible under normal use. The implementation of Dual Injection solves long-term carbon issues, and the eVANOS system is highly reliable. However, the XM introduces a vastly complex High-Voltage Plug-in Hybrid system. While the internal combustion engine is highly robust, the vehicle's lifespan is heavily tied to the longevity of the massive high-voltage battery and the electric motor integrated into the transmission.)", turboType: "Bi-Turbocharged (Equipped with two massive Twin-Scroll turbochargers nestled in the 'Hot-V' valley. The S68 utilizes a cross-bank exhaust manifold that perfectly balances exhaust pulses to completely eliminate turbo lag. The turbo system also features electric blow-off valves. When combined with the instant torque of the electric motor, it delivers a staggering 800Nm of combined torque starting immediately off idle.)", ecuType: "Bosch (A highly advanced, heavily encrypted engine management system controlling the Twin-Scroll turbos, eVANOS, Dual Injection, and the complex High-Voltage PHEV integration. Tuning an XM requires a physical bench unlock—often requiring the ECU to be shipped to FEMTO in Finland—before OBD flashing platforms can be utilized.)", euroStandard: "Euro 6e", maxPowerStockInternals: "850 - 1000+ hp (The S68 block is built to handle absolutely massive power. The closed-deck block, forged crankshaft, and robust connecting rods are legendary. With the addition of factory Port Injection, the fueling system no longer bottlenecks tuning. Once the ECU is FEMTO-unlocked, a simple software flash safely extracts immense power, further amplified by the hybrid electric motor.)",
